<title>MEXICO: Mexico OKs Wal-Mart takeover of Cifra.</title>
<headline>Mexico OKs Wal-Mart takeover of Cifra.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Monopolies Commission (CFC) announced on Thursday it had no objections to U.S.-based Wal-Mart Stores Inc acquiring control of Mexican retail chain Cifra.</p>
<p>&quot;The CFC has ruled not to object nor to attach conditions to the merger,&quot; a CFC statement said.</p>
<p>The CFC statement noted the deal aimed at raising the retail group's productivity as well as to handing over control.</p>
<p>Wal-Mart announced on June 3 it had reached a $1.2 billion deal to acquire Cifra and joint ventures Cifra-Mart and WHMC de Mexico.</p>
<p>((-- Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9562))</p>
